         "step": 1,
         "text": "The relation gives \\( f'(0) = 1 \\). Differentiate the relation, using the product rule on each term that holds \\( f \\): \\( f'' = - f - f' x \\), then \\( f''' = - 2 f' - f'' x \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Evaluate in order at \\( x = 0 \\), feeding each value into the next: \\( f'(0) = 1 \\), \\( f''(0) = -1 \\), \\( f'''(0) = -2 \\).",
         "mathjson": -2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Divide each value by the matching factorial: \\( \\frac{1}{0!} = 1 \\), \\( \\frac{1}{1!} = 1 \\), \\( \\frac{-1}{2!} = -\\frac{1}{2} \\), \\( \\frac{-2}{3!} = -\\frac{1}{3} \\).",
